  "narrative": "Starting from a distressed ULCC reference class, the Altman Z-score indicates elevated risk, but substantial liquidity and a near-term Verizon deal compress near-term risk. The net Bayesian update yields a 79% probability of bankruptcy before May 1, 2026, with calibration reflecting both strong distress signals and strong mitigants, and some sector-wide uncertainty.",
